Kruger National Park (KNP) is located in the northeastern part of South Africa and stretches along the border with Mozambique to the east, Zimbabwe to the north, and the Crocodile River to the south.
The park covers an area of 19,500 square kilometers and is divided into 14 distinct environmentally friendly zones, each supporting different wildlife species.
It is one of the most attractive tourist destinations in South Africa, and it is also considered a significant site of the South African National Parks (SANParks).
The park collects daily maintenance fees and entrance fees, just like other national parks in South Africa.
In addition, it may also benefit those who purchase the Wild Card, which grants access to any national park of their choice in South Africa and all national parks throughout South Africa.
